# ── Derived / downloaded data (regenerable — do NOT commit) ───────────────────
# The repo already carries ~300MB of parquet in history and .git is ~950MB;
# everything below rebuilds from the fetch/backtest scripts in seconds-to-minutes.
*.parquet
*.zip

# Lambda build trees (contain compiled .so)
build/
refresh_build/
*.so

# Bulk price panels (rebuild: fetch_broad.py / fetch_longhistory.py / fetch_gap_data.py)
data/carter_mastering_the_trade/backtests/risk_architecture/broad_history/
data/carter_mastering_the_trade/backtests/risk_architecture/polygon_history/

# Per-trade dumps (rebuild by rerunning the study that emits them)
data/carter_mastering_the_trade/backtests/opening_gap/gap_trades.csv

# ── Root-level backtest/study output (regenerable — do NOT commit) ────────────
# ~148MB of these got staged on 2026-08-08. Every one rebuilds from a script that
# IS committed (run_track2_pull.py, run_xsp_spread_v2.py, run_calendar.py, ...).
# Scoped to the repo root on purpose: 237 CSVs under data/ and backtests/ are
# curated inputs or published results and stay tracked.
/*.csv

# Keep small curated root files that happen to be .csv by adding them explicitly:
#   git add -f <file>

# Trade journal generated output (run_trade_review_pages.py / run_daily_journal.py) --
# deployed to CloudFront via deploy_trade_journal.sh, not meant to live in git.
# journal_trade_reviews (MySQL) is the source of truth; this is a rebuildable artifact.
data/journal/
data/cache/calendar_path/
data/cache/calendar_path_clean/
data/cache/calendar_path_clean_stk/
data/cache/calendar_path_long/
data/cache/vrp_panel/
data/cache/skew_vertical/
data/cache/shortdte_names/
data/cache/call_grid/
data/cache/intraday_hist/
# Per-trade dumps under data/studies/ that are too big to version. Each rebuilds from its
# committed script; the study's .md and *_summary_*.csv carry the result. 2026-09-23: a 59MB
# tenor_window CSV was swept in by `git add -A data/studies` and GitHub rejected it at 50MB.
# Check with `run_index_audit.py`, which now fails on any tracked file over 20MB.
data/studies/tenor_window_calls_2026-09-23.csv
data/studies/pullback_entry_events.csv
data/journal/logs/

# ── Evening-desk / scanner outputs in data/watchlist/ (regenerated every run — do NOT commit) ──
# 2026-09-24 housekeeping: these kept the working tree permanently dirty. Producers: daily_desk.sh,
# run_adhikary_scan.py, run_scan_clusters.py, run_preferred_breakouts.py (and the preferred-breakout-eod
# Lambda, whose copies live in s3://gmerton-stock-data/breakouts/), run_putspread_scan.py, run_premarket_*.py.
# Hand-edited files in data/watchlist/ (levels.csv, universe_*.txt, thesis_log.md, trade_plan_*.md,
# monitor_custom.json, ...) stay tracked. Dated files already in git stay as history (two are cited by studies).
data/watchlist/*_latest.csv
data/watchlist/*_latest.json
data/watchlist/straddle_scan_latest.txt
data/watchlist/adhikary_*20[0-9][0-9]-*.txt
data/watchlist/alerts_20[0-9][0-9]-*.csv
data/watchlist/clusters_20[0-9][0-9]-*
data/watchlist/eod_20[0-9][0-9]-*.txt
data/watchlist/positions_20[0-9][0-9]-*.txt
data/watchlist/regime_20[0-9][0-9]-*.txt
data/watchlist/straddle_screen_20[0-9][0-9]-*.txt
data/watchlist/putspread_scan*_20[0-9][0-9]-*.csv
data/watchlist/premarket_industries_20[0-9][0-9]-*.csv
